overset{\\to }{RP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/da5a61cf57c3ffcf82b693b8738334bc840a13b5f34068858e20453906d1b6f2.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RP}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c3cb5fabcbd664b0e5eef879cf54f7a5b5d0f187c2f3d68a71d3c91b972005e3.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QP} & =\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RP} \\\\  & =a+c+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f3dadde-8c2a-52fb-9b2f-2115950e19ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379767} {:answer/id #uuid "f520879e-a46a-51fd-833b-92994cba0554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379768} {:answer/id #uuid "75414c4a-acd4-5323-803d-4baf37dd6aa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379769} {:answer/id #uuid "522456cd-d0ba-5553-ae05-ca2616c89b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379770} {:answer/id #uuid "63dd52ec-958c-5fae-b4f8-cfe12c17afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "522456cd-d0ba-5553-ae05-ca2616c89b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379770} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b95c2de-263b-5af2-aa69-f0c7002ddb6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37bd86a2-0eb2-54c7-8fb4-a4d1dcc45a2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142284" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/b162564c1a2ba7f963986afb6ccbfc187769c9d04204e51dbed6afe9bcee976c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{SP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}$ in terms of $a,b$ and $c.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/821f008f5c77a2b632794077eca4da1405fe9dd77d1dd000176c5fba99a8fd98.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/4fb266a59e1d2a8ec28c4f304d05b19aa678346e429f91669590f47e9c15c9da.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70d3d01c-caa9-52b0-af1d-e5f6290aeffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379774} {:answer/id #uuid "17ac5650-fd25-57fe-950d-c9f4e189830e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379775} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cb6008-8116-514d-aad1-8151a3773c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=a-b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379776} {:answer/id #uuid "4619c372-955e-5f03-bf21-b71362b154e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=a+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379777} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc73b8c-6a72-5726-90cb-026b811255bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70d3d01c-caa9-52b0-af1d-e5f6290aeffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{PT}=a+b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379774} :answer-field/id #uuid "a52f639d-787c-57c7-9bc9-26811d10b124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6559347-eaf8-5dc7-aed6-a638ac164854" :question/math-academy-id "q-142977" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/b12b053e195f242bdf15499ee38f9b00830cd9d2a51e17a7df15ccf427b9f9c2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{PT}$ in terms of $a,b,$ and $c.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PT}=\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/f5a772ed6d71bb8654fc4fc1ad6be444c6c12827b5d582cec1af18b3329ecfb9.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/ad3812200ad6af06a69d8f105c8161b7a772512a5c2ad07e12756256663f20a6.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PT} & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a7940ef-928d-5a4f-b69d-557ca1b26337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379781} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb6eb01-447d-5a43-8fa0-f1b8596bacd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+b+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379782} {:answer/id #uuid "3a35f015-7893-54e7-869e-95fab255b30e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379783} {:answer/id #uuid "d1372472-7804-588d-a6c5-52418c2b2255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379784} {:answer/id #uuid "a92b5349-7393-527d-860d-9e8da5fdac6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a92b5349-7393-527d-860d-9e8da5fdac6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379785} :answer-field/id #uuid "067325e2-7faf-536d-a071-b7d1f3947669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c61497a-8d5a-5744-980d-520a5c733c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-142999" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c61b5aec221dd257c507fdaa8f2a04f0f29b158a6ea93afd38a310fc1150669d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ST}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $S$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/abd73b231ee79396e64c018ccfaed752efff4bedc053b1d9977761c283a3b994.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ST}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TP}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c560ab74e5d87c51adb19c287b1e75aa2ee112170f3e6361e1b5bc65c182dbda.png)\n\n   \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =b+d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "204feacf-4351-5efa-9843-c88c75572919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310338} {:answer/id #uuid "3b932b3c-c1c4-5f2e-b221-42811afb8ac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310339} {:answer/id #uuid "ab87e7b6-42c0-50cc-a2ff-35fac8a9b477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310340} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8d2b0d-f7ce-55d9-bad3-8d39140d968f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310341} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c676e5-264a-5371-b404-76ce0d09db27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab87e7b6-42c0-50cc-a2ff-35fac8a9b477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310340} :answer-field/id #uuid "8952f018-a146-5362-bace-0ef081b69d07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7320ef7f-a03e-518d-a18e-7611299ef563" :question/math-academy-id "q-143001" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" :question/worked-solution "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce8a804-6496-5bb9-a268-0eaa67aca621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310345} {:answer/id #uuid "90a591af-968f-5bf0-8335-16828df05dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310346} {:answer/id #uuid "87be4317-b9b7-5031-ad29-f9c6cb78bfa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310347} {:answer/id #uuid "8c37c2e7-b1dc-5e1f-b29e-7d7d21b8d4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310348} {:answer/id #uuid "fb20b5a3-56e4-50c3-ae66-1d5477a6c0df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb20b5a3-56e4-50c3-ae66-1d5477a6c0df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310349} :answer-field/id #uuid "110a6969-1c4c-5663-bc1e-1e533eb59026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72a6419d-1699-5afc-b525-4d434382a0f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-143006" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF} & =\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{FA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+(\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{ED})+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c43200-991b-5854-be1d-fa9db80f3725" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dea8b1e2-5c3b-5aaa-b2f0-a3528c417c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310365} {:answer/id #uuid "3db78896-d0f1-5cce-a610-5fc6317807b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dea8b1e2-5c3b-5aaa-b2f0-a3528c417c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310365} :answer-field/id #uuid "e351ee66-0add-5f2c-8052-3aeed686e669" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c081346a-0e68-599c-87e2-af148437aebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-328086" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036f7d60-0c00-5106-9777-fedb414ccbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379788} {:answer/id #uuid "1352e83e-f4d4-54ca-8eae-a2912c6d9159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b-d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "036f7d60-0c00-5106-9777-fedb414ccbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379788} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e7162f8-23a0-5516-af25-43a40abbf385" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "756dee62-4d80-5190-a3c9-f99a72aaaf64" :question/math-academy-id "q-328099" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/40fa465ab7fc211d2e4a9bb8640e12d3bb2d694eae834f514c66e53dc11fd96d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{ST}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=d,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SP}$ in terms of vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{SP}=$  \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $S$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SP}=\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/07aebf5a6aaa98c9ec5d4e9801dbe7d2cf3ade86573bcd8ee56db375f3e38575.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ST}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TQ}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/7c8c193472acbe72979f8a78fe9bd02726ad98c166381434175d0586bb574cb6.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SP} & =\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =a+b+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b921be5b-4f62-5f6a-974a-79cf76247558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b921be5b-4f62-5f6a-974a-79cf76247558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b-c+d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379792} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f526aab-899a-502b-8422-5fa283ab2180" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cb1952e-6c90-5211-bdb3-220f93fd9603" :question/math-academy-id "q-335529" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/6e5d4cef21454855d29639d236ead4c2ad6cfcb66d2b8adaa7df16405f6d250c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{TR}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{MP}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{MT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QR}=$   \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $R$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QR}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c42a0b8323c282a573244591d900801194f2f5b7382aabe60dedd903b896a029.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PM}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{MT}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/9876c3c4947aa9d61e687138bfb6fb26040e7c334af8b02914f5857ae1616e98.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QR} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR} \\\\  & =b-c+d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e49c4e36-03ae-5af4-b3ae-1705d59de6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379795} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1ee520-5f5d-57a5-8db7-59ef92d72e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b+c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e49c4e36-03ae-5af4-b3ae-1705d59de6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+b-c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379795} :answer-field/id #uuid "359e32cc-1f0f-5097-8941-56dd88aab73f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc651ec3-a7da-5cf2-ab2b-a70160d383a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-335530" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/2a4aa0aea855c84afb701ed5746dd8aa64c7644990a858a3f554014880b5657c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=b,$ and  $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ in terms of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ and $c.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=$   \n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=\\overset{\\to }{PT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/6bfe5ad7a1695d5208504f1666014737b020976d73419f4be273b5a84097e242.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PT}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/86a8fb7563c4a8874fc6d9b460c8e93bcf2c96e1b4e63a4f56f49f7326d2dcca.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{PT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RQ} \\\\  & =b-c+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe6ef57c-9154-5384-bedf-38b38637a027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310379} {:answer/id #uuid "95007e16-efe4-5ab3-81b2-5183c45f5eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310380} {:answer/id #uuid "8439cc2a-f4be-5d0b-9a73-21560f74171e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310381} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c11c8-0feb-5cce-95c0-b09f7947e32a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310382} {:answer/id #uuid "0db09e0d-65e4-5d31-b355-ef0ea2526827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c11c8-0feb-5cce-95c0-b09f7947e32a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310382} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e437920-4dba-5cd2-81e5-92329f33c30a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fba8117-2a8c-5edb-aca0-764fe3cd4be5" :question/math-academy-id "q-69539" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/86aac25c634d29639329ae53209141ce81a3a82a70d42a4c2dfc6d356ee378b8.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$" :question/worked-solution "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef54e2e4-dc52-5619-94c4-caa686b8b145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310386} {:answer/id #uuid "9e12094c-afb0-5486-a21c-a9a083956bec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310387} {:answer/id #uuid "d6eb5c9c-3776-52e4-a780-e90b1f997c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310388} {:answer/id #uuid "40648d0b-2983-5172-807f-84497531b6f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310389} {:answer/id #uuid "146a87b4-434d-5630-a3aa-9e5a5d1f39da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40648d0b-2983-5172-807f-84497531b6f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310389} :answer-field/id #uuid "16c76cba-0957-593a-9204-b41e1ddd42a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9cd0ffdc-db96-54d0-a5a8-0ff0a6ddcfc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77389" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$" :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}]}
